-- A month's salary by the law (MMS-525): what the salary calculator asks.
-- The client, 2026-10-22: "if a teacher wants to know his salary he wants
-- to know the law, he doesn't care about the underlying documents."
--
-- The takanon's §1.1 says what a teaching employee's salary is made of
-- (`salary of a teaching employee`). Here each of those components is
-- the law's answer where the root has one: the root (l4/lib/root.l4) asks
-- every instrument that speaks to the component and applies precedence.
-- A component no pay item of the shared vocabulary stands for yet is
-- §1.1's own figure, and says so (`answered by the root`): the root does
-- not know what the later instruments say about it.
--
-- Nothing here re-encodes a rule: §1.1's components are §1.1's functions,
-- and the law's answer is the root's.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `root`
IMPORT `takanon-1-1`

§ `השכר לחודש לפי הדין`

§§ `המקרה`

-- The case the root is asked about, for a salary month as §1.1 describes
-- it: the month, the 5% step's population and the two amounts §1.1
-- computes come from the month, so that the form asks each fact once.
-- "תוספת 2001" is §1.1's 3% supplement, as §1.1ד reads it.
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case` @desc the facts of the case §1.1 does not ask about
      m IS A `salary month` @desc the salary month, as §1.1 describes it
GIVETH A `teaching case`
DECIDE `the case of the month` c m IS
    `teaching case` WITH
        `the salary month`                IS m's `month`
        `employer`                        IS c's `employer`
        `in post-primary education`       IS c's `in post-primary education`
        `in the upper division`           IS c's `in the upper division`
        `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation` IS c's `represented by the secondary teachers' organisation`
        `in a population whose 5% step was put off` IS m's `in a population whose 5% step was postponed`
        `combined salary today`           IS `combined salary` m
        `supplement 2001 today`           IS `3% supplement` m
        `combined salary in December 2007` IS c's `combined salary in December 2007`
        `supplement 2001 in December 2007` IS c's `supplement 2001 in December 2007`
        `the kind of school`               IS c's `the kind of school`
        `the interns the teacher mentors`  IS c's `the interns the teacher mentors`
        `the classes in each grade`        IS c's `the classes in each grade`
        `the roles the teacher holds`      IS c's `the roles the teacher holds`
        `a further role approved by the district manager` IS c's `a further role approved by the district manager`

§§ `הרכיבים`

-- §1.1's components, in the text's order (א–ה); the percentage allowances
-- (ו) are computed on them and follow.
`§1.1's components` MEANS
    LIST `the combined salary`, `the 3% supplement`, `the 2008 supplement`,
         `the 2011 supplement`, `the 1994 teaching-agreement supplement`

-- The pay item of the shared vocabulary that a component is, where there
-- is one: the takanon's own claim on the 2008 supplement is §1.1ג's
-- (`the 2008 supplement according to the takanon`).
GIVEN s IS A `salary component`
GIVETH A MAYBE `pay item`
DECIDE `the pay item of` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `the 2008 supplement` THEN JUST `the 2008 public-sector supplement`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN s IS A `salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `answered by the root` s IS
    CONSIDER `the pay item of` s
    WHEN JUST i THEN TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- §1.1's own figure for a component.
GIVEN s IS A `salary component`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `§1.1's figure for` s m IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `the combined salary`                    THEN `combined salary` m
    WHEN `the 3% supplement`                      THEN `3% supplement` m
    WHEN `the 2008 supplement`                    THEN `2008 supplement` m
    WHEN `the 2011 supplement`                    THEN `2011 supplement` m
    WHEN `the 1994 teaching-agreement supplement` THEN `1994 supplement` m

@export A component of a teaching employee's salary for a month: the law's answer where the root has one, else section 1.1's figure
GIVEN s IS A `salary component` @desc the component
      c IS A `teaching case` @desc the facts of the case §1.1 does not ask about
      m IS A `salary month` @desc the salary month, as §1.1 describes it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the component that governs` s c m IS
    CONSIDER `the pay item of` s
    WHEN JUST i THEN
        -- no instrument gives the item to this case
        CONSIDER `the answer that governs` i (`the case of the month` c m)
        WHEN JUST a THEN a
        WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `§1.1's figure for` s m

@export A teaching employee's salary for a month, by the law: section 1.1's components, each the law's answer where the root has one, and the percentage allowances held
GIVEN c IS A `teaching case` @desc the facts of the case §1.1 does not ask about
      m IS A `salary month` @desc the salary month, as §1.1 describes it
      `the allowances held` IS A LIST OF `allowance held` @desc the percentage allowances held that month, with their rates
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary that governs` c m `the allowances held` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the component that governs` s c m) `§1.1's components`)
        PLUS `percentage allowances` m `the allowances held`

§§ `הנימוק`

-- Why the law gives what it gives for a pay item in the month: its answer,
-- the instrument that governs and the rule of precedence by which it does,
-- and what every instrument that speaks to it says, as the page shows
-- them (a module or title of "" where no instrument speaks).
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the item's answer in the month` i c m IS
    `the answer that governs` i (`the case of the month` c m)

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the module that governs the item` i c m IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i (`the case of the month` c m)
    WHEN JUST r THEN r's `governed by`'s `module`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the title that governs the item` i c m IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i (`the case of the month` c m)
    WHEN JUST r THEN r's `governed by`'s `title`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the rule that governs the item` i c m IS
    CONSIDER `the ruling on the item` i (`the case of the month` c m)
    WHEN JUST r THEN r's `by the rule`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN ""

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the modules that speak to the item` i c m IS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `by`'s `module`) (`the claims on` i (`the case of the month` c m))

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the titles that speak to the item` i c m IS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `by`'s `title`) (`the claims on` i (`the case of the month` c m))

GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `what each says of the item` i c m IS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `answer`) (`the claims on` i (`the case of the month` c m))

-- Whether the instruments that speak give the case two or more answers.
GIVEN i IS A `pay item`, c IS A `teaching case`, m IS A `salary month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item is contradicted in the month` i c m IF
    NOT null (`the contradictions on` i (`the case of the month` c m))
